From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Segno floor-console spike <to.sasovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kiosk-shell: don't SIGSEGV on click after an HDMI HPD blip

When HDMI-A-1 drops HPD for a second (TV sleep/wake, cable knock) weston
disables the output and tears down its views. The pointer can still hold
focus on that view. The next click runs kiosk_shell_activate_view, which
dereferences view->surface unconditionally and takes the compositor down
(notify_button -> kiosk-shell.so SIGSEGV). Segno then dies with
"Error flushing display: Connection reset by peer".

Return if the view or its surface is gone. The kernel cmdline D flag
(#821) is what stops the disable; this is the crash that must not happen
if HPD still gets through.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hardware/config-specific workaround]

---
 kiosk-shell/kiosk-shell.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kiosk-shell/kiosk-shell.c b/kiosk-shell/kiosk-shell.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/kiosk-shell/kiosk-shell.c
+++ b/kiosk-shell/kiosk-shell.c
@@ -1252,13 +1252,17 @@ kiosk_shell_activate_view(struct kiosk_shell *shell,
 			  struct weston_seat *seat,
 			  uint32_t flags)
 {
-	struct weston_surface *main_surface =
-		weston_surface_get_main_surface(view->surface);
-	struct kiosk_shell_surface *shsurf =
-		get_kiosk_shell_surface(main_surface);
-	struct kiosk_shell_seat *kiosk_seat =
-		get_kiosk_shell_seat(seat);
+	struct weston_surface *main_surface;
+	struct kiosk_shell_surface *shsurf;
+	struct kiosk_shell_seat *kiosk_seat;
 
+	if (!view || !view->surface)
+		return;
+
+	main_surface = weston_surface_get_main_surface(view->surface);
+	shsurf = get_kiosk_shell_surface(main_surface);
+	kiosk_seat = get_kiosk_shell_seat(seat);
+
 	if (!shsurf || !kiosk_seat)
 		return;
 
